    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b6f499d616995e8d6eae8f4cdddf3caa4498344d574e19c5a7843658b80a3db3",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "At positive integer parameters, the random-matrix gamma-product limits defining the symmetry constants can be reorganized into finite factorial and odd-double-factorial products; layerwise p-adic valuation of those products yields exact floor-sum formulas, and geometric sampling k=[p^j x] followed by a shift of valuation scale turns the discrete formulas into a bilateral nearest-integer-square profile. Alongside the second-difference control of the normalized infinite product, this connects one family of constants to analytic continuation, local integrality certificates, and self-similar valuation limits rather than treating it only numerically.",
